{
  "$comment": [
    "Hadolint rule code -> NIST SP 800-53 mapping, ported verbatim (entry order preserved) from mitre/heimdall2. Keys are hadolint's own DL#### rules and the SC#### rules hadolint surfaces from its embedded shellcheck; one table covers both because both arrive in the same hadolint report. Do not hand-edit; re-port per the procedure below.",
    "Hadolint publishes no NIST crosswalk. This table is a curated mapping authored upstream, not an authoritative control association, and is candidate triage material rather than evidence that a control is assessed or satisfied.",
    "nistRevision is 5 because the table uses SR-3 and SR-4, which exist only at Rev 5; lookups translate to the process-wide NIST revision. SR-4 has no Rev 4 equivalent and translates to an empty list, so callers must fall back to their static-analysis default rather than emit an empty nist tag.",
    "Coverage gaps: hadolint rules added after the port, and the DL1000 parse-error pseudo-rule, are absent and fall back to the caller's static-analysis default. List current rules at https://github.com/hadolint/hadolint#rules and compare against these keys.",
    "Re-port: fetch libs/hdf-converters/src/mappings/HadolintNistMappingData.ts from mitre/heimdall2 at the commit recorded in source, confirm its sha256 matches source.sha256, then transcribe each 'RULE': 'CONTROL' pair into mappings in file order as {\"nist\": [\"CONTROL\"]}."
  ],
